    "body": "Escalated to effort:high. Claim released.\n\nThe sinker catalog case is absent on upstream/main `58cb641c`.\nThe new pins `catalog_edm_sinker::regenerates` and `catalog_edm_sinker::rebuilds` both fail with `edm/sinker: missing model/`.\nProduction code was unchanged during this run.\n\nThe shipped `Sinker EDM (ISO)` post refuses Sinker Side Burn.\n`startPreamble()` rejects this operation. `onLinear()` also rejects lateral feed moves.\nBug #3001 tracks this refusal. I linked it on #2392.\n\nThe required case must post both burns. It cannot satisfy this requirement with the current shipped post.\nThe remaining work changes posted G-code and meets the effort:high safety floor.\nI chose escalation and dropped a catalog-only patch because it could not produce the required program.\n\nNo implementation or NC output changed. No PR was opened.\nThe temporary pins were discarded. No implementation patch is held.\nThe quick gate, clippy, and mutation checks were not run because there is no fix.\nThe red pin output remains at `/tmp/2872-red-pin.txt` in this session.\n\nOverlap: PR #2963 touches `example_catalog.rs` in a different case module.\nIt does not change a sinker test function.\nThe scout located the relevant source and checked for an existing post issue.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
